From: txtyb <txtybbill@163.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: oplus: AD296: ADFR tables and TE measurement

 arm64: dts: oplus: AD296 panel: ADFR tables, SA floor table, TE measurement

 * Add qcom,dsi-qsync-mode-avr-step-fps to every timing so the DSI driver knows
   the step size each timing supports.
 * Restore the oplus,adfr-min-fps-mapping-table entries and command sequences
   for the 144 Hz and 165 Hz timings (LineageOS only ships three of them).
 * Add oplus,adfr-sa-min-fps-bl-table so the driver can pick the SA floor from
   the current backlight level.
 * Drop oplus,adfr-idle-off-min-fps and lower qsync min refresh rate to 1 Hz to
   match the stock panel configuration.
 * Clear BIT14 (software marker) in oplus,adfr-config so the driver registers
   the TE GPIO interrupt at probe time. Without it test_te never measures and
   the real panel refresh rate cannot be read.
---

